Id: sctl005w
Severity: WARN
Category: network
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set net.inet.icmp.log_redirect=0 in /etc/sysctl.conf.
References: sysctl.conf(5); sysctl(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6, SC-7; ISO 8.20; CE Secure configuration

net.inet.icmp.log_redirect is 1, so every ICMP redirect is logged.
On a network that sends them the log fills with noise, which hides
what matters and can fill the disk the logs are on. FreeBSD does not
log them unless told to:
  # sysctl -w net.inet.icmp.log_redirect=0
and keep it in /etc/sysctl.conf.
